file Makefile kept 53
| # Twenty pairs of rules that each make the other's prerequisite. Every road out
| # of `out.a` walks back to `out.a`, and the one Make takes is the one that runs
| # out of rules: `rule->in_use` strikes each link from the candidates as the
| # search passes through it, so the road is as long as the catalogue and no
| # longer, and the bottom of it takes `out.a` on trust because the makefile
| # writes it down. Both tools then drop the circular dependency that road leaves
| # and fail on the recipe, which is copying a file from nowhere.
| #
| # The size is the point. A search that answers whether a chain exists and lets
| # the plan derive it again is exponential in the number of pairs -- twenty-two
| # pairs was twenty-five seconds of it -- while GNU Make is flat, because
| # `pattern_search` keeps the road it finds.
| all: out.a
